<span id="reopen-closed-tabs-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"
></span><span
  id="reopen-closed-tabs-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="reopen-closed-tabs-section-0"
>
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">undo a close</p><h2
      id="reopen-closed-tabs-section-0"
    >
      Pick the one you meant.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Use the shortcut or the panel</h3><p>
        Press ⌘⇧T on macOS or Ctrl+Shift+T on Windows and Linux, type /reopen,
        or open the Island panel and choose an entry from Recently Closed.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Bring a group back together</h3><p>
        Closing a named group records one undo entry. Reopen it to restore its
        ordinary tabs together, including its name, member order, and pins.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep each window’s history independent</h3><p>
        Reopening in one window uses that window’s list. Use Forget for one
        entry or Clear all to remove the list.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid"
  aria-labelledby="reopen-closed-tabs-section-1"
>
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">a short second chance</p><h2
      id="reopen-closed-tabs-section-1"
    >
      Some pages can return without a reload.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>For about 30 seconds</h3><p>
        At most one eligible closed page per window can retain the same page for
        about 30 seconds. Reopening it during that time can preserve things such
        as scroll position and text you were typing without fetching the page
        again.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>After that, it may reload</h3><p>
        A still-recent entry falls back to a safe navigation snapshot or its
        URL. Page state is not guaranteed, and Blanc never silently resubmits a
        form. Loading, recording, quiet, and other ineligible pages do not
        receive the same-page recovery window.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>An undo buffer with limits</h3><p>
        Recently Closed holds up to 25 entries per window, and entries expire
        after one hour. It lives only in memory and ends when the app quits.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="reopen-closed-tabs-note-title">
  <p class="section-kicker">good to know</p><h2
    id="reopen-closed-tabs-note-title"
  >
    Private tabs never enter Recently Closed.
  </h2>
  <p>
    Closed-tab recovery is not a permanent archive or a promise to recover every
    tab exactly. Private tabs are never recorded, and closed-tab snapshots never
    go to disk or sync.
  </p>
